  "notes": "Data-driven module: with the default config only the default pipeline role is planned; everything else is checked as declared capabilities via __declared__ properties. Not checkable: the CodeStar provider list (Bitbucket/GitHub/GitHubEnterpriseServer lives in a root local), and the 'external modules' for CodeBuild/Lambda actions (module blocks are not __declared__). Limitation: an event-role policy built from a gated aws_iam_policy_document data source would not be visible (data sources are not __declared__). Review 2026-09-24: event-role prefix accepts name_prefix; source-provider check requires any one stated provider wired explicitly; action-type check drops Approval (no wiring needed when config-driven). | 2026-10-03 review: dropped 4 detail checks (CodeCommit branch/tag triggers, source providers, action types): in this data-driven design they are built from config locals that the normalised input cannot see, so no candidate could pass regardless of correctness. Role permissions also accepted from declared policy blocks (jsonencode with resource refs is unknown at plan time)."
